# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=escort (The Long Haul),
# spec=paladin:protection, style=auto, view=820x1180,touch, save=carried
# (behaves as fresh per #273 -- playbot's own port is per-run, so
# localStorage's origin never actually carries between invocations).
#
# direction.md's #7 has one prior style=auto battleground reading
# (2026-09-26, druid:restoration on flags/touch): auto never steers, so a
# healer stood at its opening position the whole match and its heals sat
# out of range. This cell asks the same question on a body auto's lack of
# steering should punish differently: a tank spec, whose kit is mitigation
# and threat rather than ranged heals, on escort -- the one map on this
# line where the passive-body losses (dodge, good-dies-in-13s) were
# already measured, but never yet under auto, and never yet under any
# tank spec on any battleground map.
open
tap battleground
tap map:escort
targets
tap class:paladin:protection
shot class-picked
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot bg-start
state
ui
play auto 90
shot mid1
state
bill
wait 3
play auto 90
shot mid2
state
bill
wait 3
play auto 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
